#+TITLE: AutoCAD creation record includes unrelated Automation instances
#+STATUS: TODO
#+PRIORITY: P1
#+TYPE: bug
#+DEPENDS: exact instance identity from COM activation
#+BRANCH: codex/fermeture-cao-20261023

* Finding
RecordCreatedProcesses in backend-autocad.lisp queries every acad.exe with
/Automation in its command line and appends every matching PID and creation
time. It does not establish that each instance was created by this run.

* Risk
The orphan sweeper trusts those records as ownership evidence. In addition,
the quit bridge attaches by ProgID; with several instances of one release,
the COM object it retrieves is not proven to be the instance this run created.
Do not use these records alone to terminate an instance during qualification.

* Required correction
Record an exact activation identity, pass it to shutdown, verify it before
closing any documents, and regression-test concurrent existing instances.
